st some parameters from  the documentation here we're actually  capping the depth of the tree to four  the learning rate eta is set to point  three for the objective we're using  softmax  and we do have to tell how many classes  that we have numclass is just how many  different labels do we have so we have  three different species of iris that  we're trying to predict here so that  value is three  that one you don't have to guess about  but the other ones are basically hyper  parameters that should be tuned and like  we said the process of hyper parameter  tuning can be very intensive  we also need to pick how many epochs are  going to run this over that's another  hyper parameter how many iterations do  you want to go uh at the most in in  training this model  so let's go ahead and define those  parameters  and now we can actually train the model  given those parameters and the number of  epochs that we want to use  and that is incredibly quick right  granted is a small data set but even so  uh xgboost is really really fast now  we'll use that trained model to make  predictions notice that we passed in the  training data here for the model and now  we're going to pass in the test data to  evaluate how well that model does in  predicting  things that it's never seen before  again really quick let's go ahead and  print those out these are basically a  list of the species predictions that it  made for each  sample in our test data  and then we can again go ahead and  measure how accurate that prediction was  so we're going to import accuracy score  from sklearn.metrics  call the accuracy score function here  given our test data and the predicted  labels so we're giving it the the known  correct values here basically from our  test data and the predicted species and  we're going to compare those predicted  species to the known correct ones and  measure the accuracy of the model  and that came out again to a perfect 1.0  so that is xg boost in a nutshell hope  you guys 